# What each Ukrainian character arrives as: the Unicode code point a caller
# writes, then the byte ukua's alphabet knows it by. tools/module/codepoints.py
# turns this into delta_codepoints_ukua.c, and refuses any byte the alphabet
# (ukua.statements, edited through tools/module/alphabet.py) does not name.
#
# The 33 Cyrillic letters sit on latin-1 byte slots that Italian filled with
# accented Latin -- the chassis was Italian and Ukrainian has no use for those
# -- repurposed record by record with `alphabet.py set'. A capital arrives as
# its own lower-case byte, so the engine never sees a capital to fold and the
# convert_to_lowercase path has nothing to get wrong.

# lower-case letters
0430 c0   # а
0431 c1   # б
0432 c2   # в
0433 c3   # г
0491 c4   # ґ
0434 c5   # д
0435 c6   # е
0454 c7   # є
0436 c8   # ж
0437 c9   # з
0438 ca   # и
0456 cb   # і
0457 cc   # ї
0439 cd   # й
043a ce   # к
043b cf   # л
043c d0   # м
043d d1   # н
043e d2   # о
043f d3   # п
0440 d4   # р
0441 d5   # с
0442 d6   # т
0443 d8   # у
0444 d9   # ф
0445 da   # х
0446 db   # ц
0447 dc   # ч
0448 dd   # ш
0449 de   # щ
044c df   # ь
044e 86   # ю  -- byte 86 (Polish's ł slot, code 0xd2): a clean "own letter"
          #    routed through pol_test_own_letters. NOT à(e0) (Italian's accented
          #    a, stripped to bare a) and NOT ą(82)/ę(84): those are Polish's
          #    nasal vowels, handled by the phone default + is_sival, so they
          #    never reach the own-letter arm chain and the ju/ja rules go unrun.
044f 87   # я  -- byte 87 (Polish's ń slot, code 0xd3), same reasoning as ю

# capitals, each onto the byte of its own lower-case letter
0410 c0   # А
0411 c1   # Б
0412 c2   # В
0413 c3   # Г
0490 c4   # Ґ
0414 c5   # Д
0415 c6   # Е
0404 c7   # Є
0416 c8   # Ж
0417 c9   # З
0418 ca   # И
0406 cb   # І
0407 cc   # Ї
0419 cd   # Й
041a ce   # К
041b cf   # Л
041c d0   # М
041d d1   # Н
041e d2   # О
041f d3   # П
0420 d4   # Р
0421 d5   # С
0422 d6   # Т
0423 d8   # У
0424 d9   # Ф
0425 da   # Х
0426 db   # Ц
0427 dc   # Ч
0428 dd   # Ш
0429 de   # Щ
042c df   # Ь
042e 86   # Ю  -> ю's byte
042f 87   # Я  -> я's byte

# the combining acute the stress dictionary writes after a stressed vowel,
# and the two apostrophes that stand in for the hard sign before iotated
# vowels -- both folded onto the plain apostrophe the alphabet already names
0301 e2   # combining acute accent (stress mark)
2019 27   # right single quotation mark -> apostrophe
02bc 27   # modifier letter apostrophe -> apostrophe
